    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12387130/comment/12563515",
          "id": "12563515",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Attached patch that fixes the original bug (LUCENE-1068) by default, but offers system property & static method to keep backwards compatible yet buggy behavior.\n\nI'll commit in a day or two.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2008-01-29T13:29:43.559+0000",
          "updated": "2008-01-29T13:29:43.559+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12387130/comment/12563548",
          "id": "12563548",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=gsingers",
            "name": "gsingers",
            "key": "gsingers",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Grant Ingersoll",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Not necessarily related, but can you think of a way that we can keep WikipediaTokenizer and StandardTokenizer in sync for these kind of things.  I guess I need to go look in JFlex to see if there is a way to do inheritance.  Essentially, I want the WikiTokenizer to be StandardTokenizer plus handle the Wiki syntax appropriately.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=gsingers",
            "name": "gsingers",
            "key": "gsingers",
            "avatarUrls": {
